abstract = {Publisher Summary
This chapter discusses the system of apodeictic moods. The three moods each reducible to one another by reductio ad absurdurn are written in a column, those moods derivable from one another by the simple conversion of premises or conclusion are joined by “↔”, and those implied by another mood through sub alternation of premises or conclusion are joined to it by “→.” It is the laws of conversion and of the square of opposition which provide the means by which one may derive one valid assertoric mood from another. The chapter present a set of axioms sufficient for the deduction of all and only those moods with necessary premises(es) held to be valid by Aristotle. The various laws of modal subordination are also discussed in the chapter.}
}
